// A 2/2 vanilla carrying ward {X} with a where-X definition ([CR#702.21b]
// — Minthara, Merciless Soul's shape: "ward {X}, where X is the number of
// experience counters you have"). No canon-slice card carries ward-{X}, so
// this minimal carrier isolates the RESOLUTION-TIME pricing: the toll's
// `Mana([Variable])` is priced from the conferred ability's `where_x`
// when the ward trigger resolves, never locked in as it triggers.
Normal(
    name: "Ward X Creature",
    mana_cost: [Generic(1), White],
    types: [Creature],
    power: 2,
    toughness: 2,
    abilities: [Keyword(Ward(
        cost: [Mana([Variable])],
        where_x: CounterCount(You, Experience),
    ))],
)
